From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:37:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 107/113] x86_64: if branches that end in raise or another
 noreturn call are placed out of line

FPC's register allocator gives a value one live range from its first to its
last use in code order. A branch like "if bad then raise E.Create(...)" or
"else raise ..." lies between the hot parts of a routine, so every value
live around it crosses its calls and needs a callee-saved register (or is
spilled). tcgifnode now generates such a branch (one whose last statement is
a call that never returns and that has no exit, break, continue, goto or
user label) into current_procinfo.coldcode; psub places it after the code
that loads the return value, behind a jump to the epilogue, and registers
its register uses again so that live ranges extend to it. Only with the
setjmp based exception handling (not win64 SEH, not DWARF EH).
vm2: Op and A in registers (cycles about -6%); tests/test/opt/tcoldraise1.pp.
---
